.TH "RAPTOR-SWEEP" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-sweep \- Run MODEL once per combination of the \-\-vary values (a cartesian product), on copies, and tabulate the metrics.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor sweep\fR [\-h] \-\-vary SPEC [\-\-metric NAME] [\-f {text,json,csv}] [\-n N] [\-t T] [\-\-stop KIND[=VALUE]] [\-\-stats\-start T] [\-\-seed N] [\-j N] [\-\-timeout DURATION] [\-\-analysis LIST] [\-\-importance MODE] [\-\-weak\-type TYPE] [\-s PATH=VALUE] [\-\-set\-file FILE] [\-\-save\-model PATH] MODEL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run MODEL once per combination of the \-\-vary values (a cartesian product), on copies, and tabulate the metrics.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-vary\fR \fISPEC\fR
PATH=START:STOP:STEP or PATH=v1,v2,...; repeat for a grid
.TP
\fB\-\-metric\fR \fINAME\fR
metric(s) to tabulate (default Availability); repeatable
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json|csv}\fR

.SS Run control
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-runs\fR \fIN\fR
number of runs (default: the model's)
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-length\fR \fIT\fR
run length for a time\-terminated run
.TP
\fB\-\-stop\fR \fIKIND[=VALUE]\fR
time | failures=N | cycles=N (default: the model's)
.TP
\fB\-\-stats\-start\fR \fIT\fR
start statistics at T
.TP
\fB\-\-seed\fR \fIN\fR
salt every random stream (default: Raptor's fixed seed table)
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fIN\fR
parallel workers (default 1; N>1 is reproducible but not draw\-identical to 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIDURATION\fR
give up after DURATION, e.g. 90s, 10m (default 10m); partial results are kept
.TP
\fB\-\-analysis\fR \fILIST\fR
weak,cost,capacity (replaces the model's setting); 'none' clears all
.TP
\fB\-\-importance\fR \fIMODE\fR
IEC 61078 Annex D importance measures estimated by re\-simulation: improvement (RRW, Vesely\-Fussell), risk (RAW), both (adds Birnbaum). Costs one extra batch per block, two for 'both'
.TP
\fB\-\-weak\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR
weak\-link analysis type
.SS Changing parameters (a copy; the model file is untouched unless \-\-save\-model)
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-set\fR \fIPATH=VALUE\fR
change one field, repeatable; see 'raptor help set\-paths'
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
many PATH=VALUE lines (or a TOML/JSON table)
.TP
\fB\-\-save\-model\fR \fIPATH\fR
also write the changed model to PATH
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Availability for five values of the Weibull scale.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor sweep pump.rbd \-\-vary 'block:Pump A.fail_params[1]=200:1000:200' \-n 50\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
A 2 x 2 grid as CSV.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor sweep pump.rbd \-\-vary 'system.length=1000,2000' \-\-vary 'node:Voter.k=1,2' \-f csv\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1), \fBraptor\-set\-paths\fR(7)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
success
.TP
\fB1\fR
runtime error
.TP
\fB2\fR
usage error
.TP
\fB3\fR
model invalid (validation errors)
.TP
\fB4\fR
model refused: a shape Raptor 7 cannot run
.TP
\fB5\fR
timed out or aborted; partial results written
.TP
\fB6\fR
output could not be written
.TP
\fB130\fR
interrupted (Ctrl\-C); partial results written
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_DEBUG\fR
same as \-\-debug
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_DEV_FEATURES\fR
same as \-\-dev\-features
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_CONFIG\fR
path of the settings file (same as \-\-config)
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_WORKSPACE\fR
default for \-\-workspace
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_SEED\fR
salt for every random stream (same as \-\-seed)
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
disable colour output
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME\fR
base directories
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/raptor\-studio/config.toml\fR
settings file (see raptor\-config(5))
.TP
\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/raptor\-studio/mcp\fR
default MCP server workspace
